# Unsanitized artifacts.
#
# The diagrams under docs/demos/ were generated against a real AWS account. The
# originals contain a real account number, real resource IDs, and real addressing,
# and must never be committed. Keep them outside the repo, or drop them in _raw/
# and run scripts/sanitize.py to produce the published copies.
#
# Note the patterns here are deliberately generic: an ignore rule naming the real
# account or organisation would leak exactly what it is meant to protect.
_raw/
*.raw.html
*.unsanitized.html

# Sanitizer configuration, if you keep the tokens in a file rather than the
# environment. scripts/sanitize.py reads them from env vars by default.
scripts/sanitize.local*
.env
.env.*

# Deck working files. The published PDF lives at docs/slides/slides.pdf.
*.pptx
*.key
~$*
deck-extract/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
